; layyield: the window answers while a page takes seconds to lay out
; (test/amiga/layyield.host); a new page while one is laid out is shown
; at once; no memory may be lost (the layout left halfway)
Echo >VELOX:r/layyield.txt "layyield"
; warm-up run (one-time OS allocations: fonts, CLI, ...)
Run >NIL: VELOX:velox http://127.0.0.1:8080/index.html
Wait 8
Status >ENV:vpid COMMAND=VELOX:velox
Break $vpid C
Wait 2
Delete >NIL: ENV:vpid
Avail >NIL: FLUSH
Echo >>VELOX:r/layyield.txt "mem_before " NOLINE
Avail >>VELOX:r/layyield.txt TOTAL
Echo >VELOX:r/layyield.start ""
VELOX:velox http://127.0.0.1:8080/index.html LOG=VELOX:r/layyield.log
Echo >>VELOX:r/layyield.txt "exit rc=$RC"
Avail >NIL: FLUSH
Echo >>VELOX:r/layyield.txt "mem_after " NOLINE
Avail >>VELOX:r/layyield.txt TOTAL
Echo >>VELOX:r/layyield.txt "done"
